  data: {
    LLM: 'Deal thirteen cards to each player. The leader plays a single card or a matching set, optionally completed with wild cards. Later players may pass or play the same number of cards at a higher rank. When everyone passes, the last successful raiser clears the table and leads the next combination. Play continues until players empty their hands and receive ranks.',
    Player: 'Deal thirteen cards to each player. The leader plays a single card or a matching set, optionally completed with wild cards. Later players may pass or play the same number of cards at a higher rank. When everyone passes, the last successful raiser clears the table and leads the next combination. Play continues until players empty their hands and receive ranks.',
    objective: 'Empty your hand before the other players and gain the highest table rank for the next round.',
    gameplay: 'Deal thirteen cards to each player. The leader plays a single card or a matching set, optionally completed with wild cards. Later players may pass or play the same number of cards at a higher rank. When everyone passes, the last successful raiser clears the table and leads the next combination. Play continues until players empty their hands and receive ranks.',
    keyRules: [
      'Players must match the size of the previous combination when raising.',
      'Wild cards can complete sets and are highest when played alone.',
      'End-of-round order assigns table status, creating advantages and disadvantages in the next deal.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '4-8 players use the table arrangement described for Career Poker.',
      deck: 'Dedicated deck with 8 suits of 13 cards plus four wild cards',
      equipment: 'Dedicated deck with 8 suits of 13 cards plus four wild cards, score area, and enough table space for play.',
      dealing: 'Prepare Dedicated deck with 8 suits of 13 cards plus four wild cards and deal or lay out cards according to the documented Career Poker rules before play begins.',
    },
    turnFlow: 'Deal thirteen cards to each player. The leader plays a single card or a matching set, optionally completed with wild cards. Later players may pass or play the same number of cards at a higher rank. When everyone passes, the last successful raiser clears the table and leads the next combination. Play continues until players empty their hands and receive ranks.',
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Big Two is a point-based shedding game played without a pre-hand monetary ante.',
      deal: 'The entire 52-card deck is distributed equally by the system dealer at the start of the round.',
      reveal_market: 'This is a closed-hand climbing game where all cards are held privately; no community market exists.',
      buy_market: 'Players cannot purchase or swap cards from any external area; they must succeed with their initial 13 cards.',
      buy_stock: 'The entire deck is distributed at once; no cards remain in stock to be purchased during play.',
      fold: 'Players must remain in the game until a winner has shed all cards to determine the penalty counts.',
      check: 'The game uses a climbing and passing structure rather than a vying structure with checks and bets.',
      call: 'There is no pot or bet to match in Big Two; competition is based on combination rankings.',
      bet: 'The game is scored via penalty points for cards remaining in hand rather than through wagering.',
      raise: 'There are no wagering rounds in this game, so the value of the deal cannot be increased via raises.',
      declare: 'Winning results are immediate upon playing the last card; no formal declaration phase is required.',
      reveal_hand: 'Hands remain private until individual cards are played into climbing combos; no showdown occurs.',
      award_pot: 'Points are tallied on a scorecard after each hand; there is no physical pot of assets to award.',
      play_card: 'Must match the combination type and exceed the previous rank/suit.',
      draw: 'Each player receives thirteen cards at the start and no further drawing occurs during the play phase.',
      discard: 'Every card must be shed through valid climbing combinations; there is no separate discard or waste pile.',
      pass: 'Allowed at any time during the climbing phase.',
      bid: 'Big Two does not utilize a bidding system to determine the dealer, trump, or game objectives.',
      meld: 'This is a climbing game based on beating combinations rather than creating or laying down melds.',
      go_out: 'A player wins the round automatically upon playing their final combination from hand.',
    },
    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 13 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Empty your hand before the other players and gain the highest table rank for the next round.',
      'Turn-flow example: Deal thirteen cards to each player. The leader plays a single card or a matching set, optionally completed with wild cards. Later players may pass or play the same number of cards at a higher rank. When everyone passes, the last successful raiser clears the table and leads the next combination. Play continues until players empty their hands and receive ranks.',
      'Scoring example: Losers receive penalty points based on remaining cards (1x, 2x, or 3x multipliers). First player to empty their hand wins the round..',
